  "question": {
    "text": "For integers $m$ and $n$, both greater than 1, consider the following three statements :\n$P: m$ divides $n$\n$Q: m$ divides $n^2$\n$R: m$ is prime, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4OUj5",
      "text": "\n$Q \\wedge R \\rightarrow P$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SxYe0",
      "text": "\n$P \\wedge Q \\rightarrow R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "npoCr",
      "text": "\n$Q \\rightarrow R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KfHH2",
      "text": "\n$Q \\rightarrow P$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(b) $\\frac{8}{4}=2, \\frac{64}{4}=16$; but 4 is not prime.\nHence $\\mathrm{P} \\wedge \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{R}$, false\n(c) $\\frac{(6)^2}{12}=\\frac{36}{12}=3$; but 12 is not prime Hence $Q \\rightarrow R$, false\n(d) $\\frac{(4)^2}{8}=\\frac{16}{8}=2 ; \\frac{4}{8}$ is not an integer Hence $\\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{P}$, false",
    "image": null
  },
